{"uid":"ab4cfc681fffdb75","name":"test_silent_prelude_case_renders_the_full_renderers_last_two_lines_on_both_real_paths","fullName":"tests.test_log_merge_bounded_reads#test_silent_prelude_case_renders_the_full_renderers_last_two_lines_on_both_real_paths","historyId":"9c3cc09cbf47d385bfafc169b2e2869b","time":{"start":1791959814351,"stop":1791959816634,"duration":2283},"description":"Task 014: the GENUINELY ABSENT index case -- no `render_index.json`\n    and no `collapse_index.json` at all for this iteration -- through\n    `ui_server.rendered_log_lines` itself, on both its surfaces\n    (`live=False`, the dead-run on-disk fallback, and `live=True`, the\n    live proxy branch). This used to be `ui_server`'s own disclosed\n    residual (`test_absent_index_residual_costs_measured_through_the_\n    whole_client_facing_call`, task cure-01-09/#272, now cured by this\n    task): its outer growth loop (`_fetch_live_tail`/`_fetch_dead_tail`)\n    stopped the moment a fetch's render already held `bound_tail` lines,\n    even when those lines came from a collapse-state seed `log_merge`\n    itself discloses as UNRESOLVED rather than measured (PRD Q.1) -- a\n    guessed `False` for `textSeen` that made the already-streamed text\n    replay in place of the real `[thinking...]` suffix.\n\n    This task's cure never touches `log_merge`'s own generic bounded-read\n    contract -- that residual stays exactly as it was for a caller that\n    reads `merge_entries_tail`/`merged_lines` directly (`ralphctl logs\n    --tail`), which is why this test checks ONLY `ui_server.\n    rendered_log_lines`, not the on-disk merge or the ASGI `GET /logs`\n    handler by themselves. `ui_server`'s own outer loop now refuses to\n    settle for a fetch whose seed still carries `unresolved`\n    (`_raw_text_has_unresolved_seed`) purely because it already has\n    enough rendered lines, and keeps growing -- the same doubling/full-ask\n    machinery the ordinary case already uses -- until either the flag\n    resolves or the fetch has read this iteration's entire transcript (at\n    which point there is no omitted prefix left to guess about at all).\n    Checked at both silent-prelude depths (1,000/1,700 padded silent\n    `message_end` events before the streamed text; the exact fixture\n    `_assert_silent_prelude_publishes_unknown_state_not_empty_state`\n    above already builds at both depths, minus the index write)","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 014: the GENUINELY ABSENT index case -- no <code>render_index.json</code><br />\nand no <code>collapse_index.json</code> at all for this iteration -- through<br />\n<code>ui_server.rendered_log_lines</code> itself, on both its surfaces<br />\n(<code>live=False</code>, the dead-run on-disk fallback, and <code>live=True</code>, the<br />\nlive proxy branch). This used to be <code>ui_server</code>'s own disclosed<br />\nresidual (<code>test_absent_index_residual_costs_measured_through_the_ whole_client_facing_call</code>, task cure-01-09/#272, now cured by this<br />\ntask): its outer growth loop (<code>_fetch_live_tail</code>/<code>_fetch_dead_tail</code>)<br />\nstopped the moment a fetch's render already held <code>bound_tail</code> lines,<br />\neven when those lines came from a collapse-state seed <code>log_merge</code><br />\nitself discloses as UNRESOLVED rather than measured (PRD Q.1) -- a<br />\nguessed <code>False</code> for <code>textSeen</code> that made the already-streamed text<br />\nreplay in place of the real <code>[thinking...]</code> suffix.</p>\n<pre><code>This task's cure never touches `log_merge`'s own generic bounded-read\ncontract -- that residual stays exactly as it was for a caller that\nreads `merge_entries_tail`/`merged_lines` directly (`ralphctl logs\n--tail`), which is why this test checks ONLY `ui_server.\nrendered_log_lines`, not the on-disk merge or the ASGI `GET /logs`\nhandler by themselves. `ui_server`'s own outer loop now refuses to\nsettle for a fetch whose seed still carries `unresolved`\n(`_raw_text_has_unresolved_seed`) purely because it already has\nenough rendered lines, and keeps growing -- the same doubling/full-ask\nmachinery the ordinary case already uses -- until either the flag\nresolves or the fetch has read this iteration's entire transcript (at\nwhich point there is no omitted prefix left to guess about at all).\nChecked at both silent-prelude depths (1,000/1,700 padded silent\n`message_end` events before the streamed text; the exact fixture\n`_assert_silent_prelude_publishes_unknown_state_not_empty_state`\nabove already builds at both depths, minus the index write)\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791959389113,"stop":1791959389113,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791959389113,"stop":1791959389113,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791959814328,"stop":1791959814328,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791959814329,"stop":1791959814336,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791959814336,"stop":1791959814336,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"sh